[{:db/id "q-122393/selection/941c11e924a91c46a40cccdb0ed7f13fbe15bcda84e189ec4e556d340c071164" :answer/id #uuid "78121f4f-47a1-541f-972f-e9d12f52e9b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122393/selection/9fb04510760b42e34e2430c6e927d28f4b562d94d23661100dea35436b305534" :answer/id #uuid "a187b14f-380c-54f2-8562-6442ae532af8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122393/selection/497bda384b7d53ff294b61fa8f6ac146b3a990dd83ec99ed4e8e93786c8b9ede" :answer/id #uuid "91f5bc72-7a18-54b9-a102-577832861b7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122393/selection/581e6dc1e03e7f5c60c33f8fb35f9f5e9817eba2be987da7461a25391966f435" :answer/id #uuid "b2f99572-65b3-5bf9-9c0f-a70538c178a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={cos}^{2}⁡x+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122393/selection/71bf2c0927219f5f66130453d9a44ac6a335e4df3d5f402a2ed4aad74566da36" :answer/id #uuid "607710bd-30b2-519e-b72c-a742e6794283" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122393/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b6fad4bb-6159-5bc5-8de7-a37512e9b550" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122393/selection/497bda384b7d53ff294b61fa8f6ac146b3a990dd83ec99ed4e8e93786c8b9ede" :answer-field/choices ["q-122393/selection/941c11e924a91c46a40cccdb0ed7f13fbe15bcda84e189ec4e556d340c071164" "q-122393/selection/9fb04510760b42e34e2430c6e927d28f4b562d94d23661100dea35436b305534" "q-122393/selection/497bda384b7d53ff294b61fa8f6ac146b3a990dd83ec99ed4e8e93786c8b9ede" "q-122393/selection/581e6dc1e03e7f5c60c33f8fb35f9f5e9817eba2be987da7461a25391966f435" "q-122393/selection/71bf2c0927219f5f66130453d9a44ac6a335e4df3d5f402a2ed4aad74566da36"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122393" :question/id #uuid "66e6fd67-7c2f-53c8-9b0c-0cf636baf830" :question/math-academy-id "q-122393" :question/problem "The length of a curve $y=f(x)$ is given by ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1+{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Which of the following could be  an equation for this curve?" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe're given that \n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1+{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComparing the above with the arc length formula, we see that we must have\n\n$$\n[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}={sin}^{2}⁡x\\,⟹\\,{f}^{′}(x)=\\pm \\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nIntegrating the above equation with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\pm \\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\text{ d}x \\\\  & =\\pm \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, the only one that has the required form is $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-122393/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55f783c4-25d6-5855-877e-31bed16b12c4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122393"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122394/selection/5e4e0eb698a5aa0db83aecad88d652cd16c6725ddd3fd19141699138f6cd2512" :answer/id #uuid "754835f1-9d4b-53e0-a400-3684640d06d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122394/selection/70cfd484f07404ebdb2d0701b5d20a9dabf46c7f10b4140cb544e58f20ad48b9" :answer/id #uuid "059886a4-add3-5b9b-a3bd-b7e98ac0d198" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x-\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122394/selection/d704feeb5fd34309a867f7a5735d17bfd0afefa451456c7d60906dae1dabddfa" :answer/id #uuid "4c3b78c0-ba8a-5e9e-80ee-56ab8f899fc4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{2x}{1+{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122394/selection/ea59003c3a70126b90fb2765e1d55f324d36a9cf06a530ef731e1d9bf6c78e72" :answer/id #uuid "acba5c59-3cee-58fe-9890-012edb1d687f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{x}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122394/selection/4a312aeac0e520baf52113105ae18f81acdf152048fcc464e626630456bd17a9" :answer/id #uuid "63e86edc-50b8-5fd7-8b66-8d051c370d3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122394/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "154365b8-40db-503d-a526-8c469a07ac13" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122394/selection/70cfd484f07404ebdb2d0701b5d20a9dabf46c7f10b4140cb544e58f20ad48b9" :answer-field/choices ["q-122394/selection/5e4e0eb698a5aa0db83aecad88d652cd16c6725ddd3fd19141699138f6cd2512" "q-122394/selection/70cfd484f07404ebdb2d0701b5d20a9dabf46c7f10b4140cb544e58f20ad48b9" "q-122394/selection/d704feeb5fd34309a867f7a5735d17bfd0afefa451456c7d60906dae1dabddfa" "q-122394/selection/ea59003c3a70126b90fb2765e1d55f324d36a9cf06a530ef731e1d9bf6c78e72" "q-122394/selection/4a312aeac0e520baf52113105ae18f81acdf152048fcc464e626630456bd17a9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122394" :question/id #uuid "08fd2f9a-1829-5290-b589-aa44873ab0cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-122394" :question/problem "The length of a curve $y=f(x)$ is given by ${\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{{(1+{x}^{2})}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Which of the following could be  an equation for this curve?" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe're given that \n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{{(1+{x}^{2})}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComparing the above with the arc length formula, we see that we must have\n\n$$\n[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}=\\frac{1}{{(1+{x}^{2})}^{2}}\\,⟹\\,{f}^{′}(x)=\\pm \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nIntegrating the above equation with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\pm \\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\text{ d}x \\\\  & =\\pm \\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, the only one that has the required form is $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x-\\pi .$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-122394/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55f783c4-25d6-5855-877e-31bed16b12c4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122394"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-362547/field-1/ff719fe6e9f394f14c4ef7f13ec8dc8641132e81c0acb9899b233b18e63ce753" :answer/id #uuid "2f0f2d4c-db15-5b58-ab73-173a61af05a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{38}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-362547/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ac621415-b4be-5980-9858-0303051b4ef1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-362547/field-1/ff719fe6e9f394f14c4ef7f13ec8dc8641132e81c0acb9899b233b18e63ce753" :answer-field/choices ["q-362547/field-1/ff719fe6e9f394f14c4ef7f13ec8dc8641132e81c0acb9899b233b18e63ce753"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-362547" :question/id #uuid "6f666954-7c4b-5495-9ca7-05b2d55a9a71" :question/math-academy-id "q-362547" :question/problem "Compute the arc length $L$ of $y=\\frac{2}{3}(x+2)^{3/2}$ for $x\\in [1,6].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$L=$ \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\frac{2}{3}(x+2)^{3/2},$ $a=1,$ and $b=6.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}(x+2)^{1/2}=\\sqrt{x+2}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}} & =\\sqrt{1+{[\\sqrt{x+2}]}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+(x+2)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{x+3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}=\\sqrt{x+3}$ to the formula for the arc length, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{6}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{6}\\sqrt{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{2}{3}(x+3)^{3/2})|}_{1}^{6} \\\\  & =[\\frac{2}{3}(6+3)^{3/2}]-[\\frac{2}{3}(1+3)^{3/2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{54}{3}-\\frac{16}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{38}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-362547/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f87bc14d-5e68-5a5e-bec8-f1b5b21c02e8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-362547"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
